RentNearby database migrations.

Run from the backend directory:

    flask --app run.py db upgrade

Create a new migration after changing SQLAlchemy models:

    flask --app run.py db migrate -m "Describe the schema change"
    flask --app run.py db upgrade

The initial migration includes the PostgreSQL btree_gist extension and a partial GiST exclusion constraint that prevents overlapping reserved date ranges for a product. Run migrations against PostgreSQL; SQLite is intended only for fast unit tests and does not enforce that exclusion constraint.
